---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-10-17';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Editorial policy', path: '/editorial-policy/' },
  ]}
  description="How singletenant.ai sources and verifies vendor facts, how corrections are made, and how conflicts of interest are handled."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Editorial</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Editorial policy
      </h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs mb-10" style="color: var(--color-mute);">
        Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy covers everything published on singletenant.ai: the
          vendor database, the comparisons generated from it, and the guides
          and analysis. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page
          describes how the database is built; this page sets out the rules
          the editor holds it to.
        </p>

        <h2 id="sourcing">Sourcing</h2>
        <p>
          Vendor facts come from primary sources: the vendor's own
          documentation, trust centre, legal terms, contracts published on its
          site, and pricing pages. Regulatory and legal statements in guides
          and analysis come from the regulator, the legislation, or the
          official publication itself. Press coverage, analyst summaries,
          forum threads, marketing listicles, and AI-generated summaries are
          not sources, though they can prompt a check of the primary material.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every vendor profile lists, field by field, the primary source each
          field was checked against and the date of that check, and every
          populated fact links to the specific page behind it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="verification">Verification</h2>
        <p>
          A fact is recorded as verified only when the linked primary source
          states it on the date shown. If the source is ambiguous, only implies
          the claim, or cannot be reached, the fact is recorded as "Not
          verified". It is never inferred from a related claim, a launch blog,
          or a rebrand.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each vendor profile shows a "Last verified" date: the date of the
          oldest check behind any field on the page, so the headline date never
          overstates how fresh the profile is. Individual sections carry their
          own dates. Comparison pages show the older of the two vendors' dates.
        </p>

        <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone can request a correction, vendors included, by emailing
          <a href="mailto:editor@singletenant.ai">editor@singletenant.ai</a>
          with the page, the claim, and a link to the primary source that
          contradicts it. The claim is re-checked against the vendor's
          published material. If it fails, the data is corrected, its verified
          date is updated, and the correction is logged as a dated entry in the
          <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>. Corrections are never made
          silently, and a correction request is not accepted without a primary
          source, whoever sends it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Errors in guides and analysis are corrected in place, with the
          article's updated date changed and, for any substantive error, a
          note in the text saying what changed.
        </p>

        <h2 id="conflicts">Conflicts of interest</h2>
        <p>
          No vendor can pay for inclusion, placement, ordering, or the content
          of its profile or comparisons. Commercial relationships (referral
          links, advertising, and sponsorship) are kept separate from the data
          and are listed on the <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.
          Paid placements are always labelled where they appear.
        </p>
        <p>
          The editor does not sell consulting or other services through this
          site. If the editor has a financial relationship with a vendor
          covered here, it is listed on the disclosure page, and that vendor's
          profile is not edited until the relationship is disclosed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vendors do not review or approve copy before publication. A vendor
          may point out a factual error after publication, through the same
          corrections process as any reader.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
